<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <title>CSS Colors, Gradients & Fonts Practice</title>

  <!-- ============================================================
       TASK 3: Load two Google Fonts
       - Poppins (headings)
       - Inter (paragraphs)
       ============================================================ -->
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
  <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Poppins:wght@600;700;800&family=Inter:wght@400;500&display=swap"
        rel="stylesheet">

  <!-- ============================================================
       TASK 5: Trending font for the banner headline
       - 'Bricolage Grotesque' is a modern, trendy display font
         popular in 2024-25 for youth-focused brands.
       ============================================================ -->
  <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Bricolage+Grotesque:wght@700;800&display=swap"
        rel="stylesheet">

  <style>
    /* ============================================================
       Global styling
       ============================================================ */
    * { box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0; padding: 0; }
    body {
      /* TASK 3: paragraph font = Inter */
      font-family: 'Inter', Arial, sans-serif;
      background-color: #f5f6f7;
      color: #222;
      line-height: 1.6;
      padding: 30px 20px;
    }

    /* TASK 3: ALL headings use Poppins */
    h1, h2, h3, h4, h5, h6 {
      font-family: 'Poppins', sans-serif;
      font-weight: 700;
      color: #1a1a2e;
    }

    .container {
      max-width: 900px;
      margin: 0 auto;
    }

    section {
      background-color: white;
      border-radius: 12px;
      padding: 30px;
      margin-bottom: 30px;
      box-shadow: 0 4px 14px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.05);
    }

    .section-title {
      font-size: 22px;
      margin-bottom: 20px;
      border-left: 5px solid #ff5722;
      padding-left: 12px;
    }

    /* ============================================================
       TASK 1: Three coloured boxes (RGB, HEX, named color)
       ============================================================ */
    .boxes-row {
      display: flex;
      gap: 20px;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      justify-content: center;
    }
    .box {
      width: 200px;
      height: 130px;
      border-radius: 12px;
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: center;
      color: white;
      font-family: 'Poppins', sans-serif;
      font-weight: 600;
      font-size: 15px;
      text-align: center;
      box-shadow: 0 6px 18px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.15);
      transition: transform 0.2s ease;
    }
    .box:hover { transform: translateY(-4px); }

    /* Box 1: RGB color */
    .box-rgb {
      background-color: rgb(52, 152, 219); /* medium blue */
    }
    /* Box 2: HEX color */
    .box-hex {
      background-color: #e74c3c;           /* flat red */
    }
    /* Box 3: Named color */
    .box-named {
      background-color: mediumseagreen;    /* named color */
    }

    /* ============================================================
       TASK 2 + TASK 5: Banner with linear gradient +
       Bricolage Grotesque headline
       ============================================================ */
    .banner {
      /* TASK 2: linear gradient with two+ colors */
      background-image: linear-gradient(135deg,
                        #ff5722 0%,
                        #ff9800 50%,
                        #ffc107 100%);
      color: white;                        /* TASK 2: white text for contrast */
      padding: 60px 30px;
      border-radius: 16px;
      text-align: center;
      box-shadow: 0 10px 30px rgba(255, 87, 34, 0.35);
      margin-bottom: 30px;
    }
    .banner h1 {
      /* TASK 5: Bricolage Grotesque for the headline */
      font-family: 'Bricolage Grotesque', 'Poppins', sans-serif;
      font-size: 44px;
      font-weight: 800;
      color: white;
      letter-spacing: -1px;
      margin-bottom: 12px;
      text-shadow: 0 2px 12px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.2);
    }
    .banner p {
      font-size: 17px;
      opacity: 0.95;
      margin-bottom: 22px;
      font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif;
    }
    .banner button {
      background-color: white;
      color: #ff5722;
      font-family: 'Poppins', sans-serif;
      font-weight: 700;
      font-size: 15px;
      border: none;
      padding: 13px 30px;
      border-radius: 30px;
      cursor: pointer;
      transition: transform 0.2s ease, box-shadow 0.2s ease;
    }
    .banner button:hover {
      transform: translateY(-3px);
      box-shadow: 0 10px 22px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.25);
    }

    /* ============================================================
       TASK 4: Readability — before vs after
       ============================================================ */
    .readability-demo {
      display: flex;
      gap: 25px;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
    }
    .readability-col {
      flex: 1 1 300px;
      padding: 20px;
      border-radius: 10px;
    }
    .readability-col h4 {
      font-size: 15px;
      margin-bottom: 12px;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      letter-spacing: 1px;
    }
    /* BEFORE: hard to read */
    .before-col {
      background-color: #fff5f5;
      border: 1px dashed #ffb3b3;
    }
    .before-col h4 { color: #c62828; }
    .before-text {
      /* Deliberately bad choices to show the difference */
      font-weight: 300;
      letter-spacing: -0.5px;
      line-height: 1.1;
      font-size: 14px;
      color: #555;
    }
    /* AFTER: improved readability */
    .after-col {
      background-color: #f1f8e9;
      border: 1px dashed #aed581;
    }
    .after-col h4 { color: #2e7d32; }
    .after-text {
      /* Better readability */
      font-weight: 500;          /* slightly bolder */
      letter-spacing: 0.2px;     /* subtle breathing room */
      line-height: 1.75;         /* comfortable leading */
      font-size: 15px;
      color: #333;
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>

  <div class="container">

    <!-- ============================================================
         TASK 2 + TASK 5: Banner with gradient + trending font
         ============================================================ -->
    <div class="banner">
      <h1>Craving Something? We Deliver in 15 Minutes 🛵</h1>
      <p>Fresh meals from your favourite restaurants — right to your door.</p>
      <button>Order Now</button>
    </div>

    <!-- ============================================================
         TASK 1: Three coloured boxes
         ============================================================ -->
    <section>
      <h2 class="section-title">Task 1 · Three Coloured Boxes</h2>
      <div class="boxes-row">
        <div class="box box-rgb">
          RGB<br>rgb(52, 152, 219)
        </div>
        <div class="box box-hex">
          HEX<br>#e74c3c
        </div>
        <div class="box box-named">
          Named<br>mediumseagreen
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============================================================
         TASK 3: Google Fonts demo
         ============================================================ -->
    <section>
      <h2 class="section-title">Task 3 · Google Fonts Demo</h2>
      <h3>This heading uses Poppins</h3>
      <p>
        This paragraph uses Inter. All headings on this page use the Poppins
        Google Font, and all paragraph text uses Inter for a clean,
        readable body.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- ============================================================
         TASK 4: Readability — before vs after
         ============================================================ -->
    <section>
      <h2 class="section-title">Task 4 · Readability (Before vs After)</h2>

      <div class="readability-demo">

        <!-- BEFORE column -->
        <div class="readability-col before-col">
          <h4>❌ Before</h4>
          <p class="before-text">
            Spice Route is a North Indian restaurant serving authentic biryani,
            kebabs, and curries. We use fresh ingredients and traditional
            recipes to deliver the true taste of Hyderabad to your doorstep
            every single day.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- AFTER column -->
        <div class="readability-col after-col">
          <h4>✅ After</h4>
          <p class="after-text">
            Spice Route is a North Indian restaurant serving authentic biryani,
            kebabs, and curries. We use fresh ingredients and traditional
            recipes to deliver the true taste of Hyderabad to your doorstep
            every single day.
          </p>
        </div>

      </div>

      <!-- Explanation as code comments -->
      <p style="margin-top:20px; font-size:14px; color:#555;">
        <strong>Why "After" is more readable:</strong>
      </p>
      <ul style="margin-left:20px; font-size:14px; color:#444; line-height:1.8;">
        <li><code>font-weight</code> raised from <strong>300</strong> → <strong>500</strong> so thin strokes don't disappear on smaller screens.</li>
        <li><code>letter-spacing</code> changed from <strong>-0.5px</strong> → <strong>0.2px</strong> to give letters breathing room.</li>
        <li><code>line-height</code> increased from <strong>1.1</strong> → <strong>1.75</strong> so lines don't feel cramped.</li>
        <li><code>font-size</code> bumped from <strong>14px</strong> → <strong>15px</strong> for a more comfortable reading size.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <!-- ============================================================
         TASK 5: Font choice explanation
         ============================================================ -->
    <section>
      <h2 class="section-title">Task 5 · Why "Bricolage Grotesque" for the Banner?</h2>
      <p>
        I chose <strong>Bricolage Grotesque</strong> for the banner headline because:
      </p>
      <ul style="margin-left:20px; margin-top:12px; line-height:1.9; color:#333;">
        <li><strong>Youthful &amp; trendy:</strong> It's a recent release on Google Fonts that's quickly become a favourite for modern startups, food apps, and D2C brands.</li>
        <li><strong>High impact at large sizes:</strong> Its slightly condensed, chunky letterforms feel confident and bold — perfect for a 44px headline.</li>
        <li><strong>Playful yet readable:</strong> The quirky details (like the double-storey 'a') add personality without hurting legibility.</li>
        <li><strong>Complements the gradient:</strong> Against the warm orange-yellow gradient, the heavy geometric sans holds its own and pops with a subtle text-shadow.</li>
      </ul>
      <p style="margin-top:14px; color:#555; font-size:14px;">
        For a youth-focused food app, "vibe" matters as much as function.
        Bricolage Grotesque delivers both — modern, energetic, and unmistakably now.
      </p>
    </section>

  </div>

</body>
</html>
